#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186293890 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4df33ff-e04e-55ec-b273-9eceff7db53b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Rotation Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f73592d-1a3a-58aa-be0b-c2bf22972c9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033087/assets/489bc530fc35e2e740038264f2be05bffb90214249ec5602591623d457325db3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293892} {:answer/id #uuid "b5653e6b-7125-50a8-9ac0-67659ec5449a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033087/assets/ba328088ca187ea28b241a302a486da1145a51c7e134d8d4f529f5f4a916ddc1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293893} {:answer/id #uuid "65a3beed-47ed-544c-80fd-8e3487b18804" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033087/assets/5bd4d8cc2643767b82acc0e61d168f5b387be67a7ff96634604e0d6828cc288b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293894} {:answer/id #uuid "daa88a91-2d37-5256-bdd5-2a7499c9b507" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033087/assets/efb79fc1071f79597c81a0a974e7f6b21d361ac046f728625e2fe1c02bb507eb.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293895} {:answer/id #uuid "2acb9fbd-6a13-5bc4-aa20-d80083518450" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033087/assets/2da0ffb873eb230718aab29c7dd09e015a0801b7ecb3b7dea91102f30b3e8816.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293896}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b5653e6b-7125-50a8-9ac0-67659ec5449a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033087/assets/ba328088ca187ea28b241a302a486da1145a51c7e134d8d4f529f5f4a916ddc1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293893} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c79d7c0-dfcf-5cba-beb2-f25c807802d7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293891}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "75802105-915e-5223-a4a4-b4c2831bb162" :question/math-academy-id "q-160619" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033087/assets/f3e31d1c15a97adea32790eafe75ad1bc9f70c854b516b98de6648ec8d7bcb87.png)\n\nConsider the vector $v$ shown above. Find the vector $Av$ given that \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Consider the standard basis ${i,j}$ of the Euclidean plane ${R}^{2}$ and the unit square spanned by the vectors. Computing the images of ${i,j}$ under $A$, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{i}^{′} & =A(i)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=-i \\\\ {j}^{′} & =A(j)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=-j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we obtain the following diagram:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033087/assets/9fae3ec0ada3008937d88e4e76374a56da4369b1821cfee072c90d88b562df46.png)\n\nSo, the matrix represents a rotation of $\\pi $ radians (counterclockwise or clockwise) about the origin.\n\nTherefore, in order to find $Av$, we need to rotate $v$ (counterclockwise or clockwise) by an angle of $\\pi $ radians, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033087/assets/ae800b271848948b5f60f5cd7c1cecd163c2aa7399e9a87e2a52d158857c6a42.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186293897 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4df33ff-e04e-55ec-b273-9eceff7db53b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Rotation Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a451e005-9920-55ba-aba2-4a82df7fdc89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033087/assets/4a78a3e98da4c602b4e8a2ebbe8860f75e507ec2ec5c20df0e59100f96a099ac.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293899} {:answer/id #uuid "12c5a080-b22a-52c1-9b3c-1e3a4833e96d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033087/assets/cf86cad03c80018ac3976a64780650c827d7c93a0889286c711c5aa69d2b899f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293900} {:answer/id #uuid "1bef1177-6e7a-54d6-8454-e86c89efdb92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033087/assets/f2beba76039ead47c83c93aaad5f9c4717a4abd2b803e65157f23d770f4f9181.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293901} {:answer/id #uuid "4504772e-8da4-5cff-a3c3-c6172ca608b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033087/assets/3edafbd6273f8058114c606c8b2a288e52b348d560867b6ea90e8b981b486904.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293902} {:answer/id #uuid "5e6b05d3-925f-5dad-adbd-f539eb186ef1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033087/assets/82091407834f5d7aa8caf6e01cb800a3f7b1999cb0c6e568c899d43479b1d7a3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293903}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a451e005-9920-55ba-aba2-4a82df7fdc89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033087/assets/4a78a3e98da4c602b4e8a2ebbe8860f75e507ec2ec5c20df0e59100f96a099ac.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293899} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c52ba30-782e-5f65-9f49-6868e4cb05f7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293898}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "efaa3158-b486-5ce8-9ecd-d7b2e13036d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-160621" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033087/assets/b75a7519c7953b7a3c5bd5b5e61e961ca26c3f0dc9e1aab32bf2c639dd95325f.png)\n\nConsider the vector $v$ shown above. Find the vector $Av$ given that \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Consider the standard basis ${i,j}$ of the Euclidean plane ${R}^{2}$ and the unit square spanned by the vectors. Computing the images of ${i,j}$ under $A$, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{i}^{′} & =Ai=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=j \\\\ {j}^{′} & =Aj=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=-i\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we obtain the following diagram:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033087/assets/f154267ed0a528b1e9fbec40064b090560410fe76dab00070e13fb3d1978b59c.png)\n\nSo, the matrix represents a rotation of $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ radians counterclockwise about the origin.\n\nTherefore, in order to find $Av$, we need to rotate $v$ counterclockwise by an angle of $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ radians, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033087/assets/8ea257c65769c4d6f67f55ce6533c1bfdfe45debcf1ba532b9ec3f717238507a.png)"}]}
